  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.5.$ This means that $k=1.5$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}+1.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,3.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}+1.5 \\\\ 3.5 & =\\frac{a}{1}+1.5 \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+k=2+1.5=3.5.$",
